    l_b/l      l_b  l_b/dx   peak load  normalised     W_rel    W_curv  reached  cuts
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   class.   0.0000      --      0.3742      1.0000         0         0    1.000     0
     0.00   0.0000      --      0.3705      0.9900  0.000217         0    0.875     0
     2.00   0.2000     8.0      0.3772      1.0078   0.00157   0.00158    0.875     0

    --to-peak: 2 of 3 rows stopped once the load had fallen to 90% of
    their own maximum. The peak load and the three shares are evaluated at the
    peak, so they are unaffected; the post-peak branch and the damage figures
    are not available from this run.

    Peak load varies by 1.80% across the whole sweep, and the curvature
    share of the driving force never exceeds 1.6e-03. The internal length is not
    reaching the crack. This is not a deficiency of the formulation: the wryness
    measures the *gradient* of the microrotation, a notched plate in tension is
    stretch-dominated, so that gradient is small however l_b compares with the
    notch, the specimen or l. Compare notched_beam, where the same machinery in
    bending moves the peak load substantially.

