    Geometry, mesh, l and G_c are identical across every row, so a classical model
    -- having no length of its own -- returns one curve for all of them. Here the peak
    load changes by 3.56x, and the curvature share of the damage driving force
    rises from 0.0e+00 to 0.446: the couple stress carries load the
    classical beam has to shed into damage.
    Monotone in l_b: True. Two points could be a coincidence of parameters;
    a monotone sweep is the statement that l_b is what is doing the work.

